WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Good morning John! It occurs to me that there are a lot of things that I haven't haven't told you about in my life.

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.000
So, I want to make a video in which we catch up.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.500
Thing number 1

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.820
You may remember a while back that Katherine and I were fostering a greyhound in the hopes that we would

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.880
get to keep her. However, when the people at the adoption agency came by to see how she was doing,

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:19.640
and saw the way that she was looking at our cat

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.380
(Which is apparently the way, that you know,

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.760
I look at a quarter-pounder double-stacked with cheese from Wendy's)

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:26.260
They said that that particular dog would have to find a home

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:29.600
that did not have little furry friends living in it

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:33.020
which has already happened, and that wonderful dog has a wonderful home down the valley

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.140
So Katherine and I had to wait for a bunch of time for a new shipment

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.940
of retired racing greyhounds to come into Missoula, which they did

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:42.260
and we adopted this lovely dog, who is extremely sweet.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.780
Her track name was Tina Fey, and we have named her Lemon.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:47.060
And she's sleeping right next to me right now

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.180
(high-pitched) There she is!

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.920
She likes to be as close to us as possible

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.440
Thing number 2

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.440
Retired racing greyhounds are really great dogs,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.960
and if you're in the market for a new dog,

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:59.480
you should check and see if there is an adoption agency that specializes in greyhounds nearby you

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:02.500
because there are a lot of greyhounds that retire from tracks,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.400
and are not able to get adopted into homes

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.620
Thing number 3

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:11.120
After Lemon poops, she just, she's the happiest-it's the happiest time of her day.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.400
Which makes me very nostalgic for the days in which I used to enjoy...pooping.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.820
But on a good note, I have been feeling much better lately,

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:20.840
and have managed to get a new prescription for a new kind of drug,

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:22.600
which is like half as much as the old one.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:27.760
The price of my drugs, went from $385 a month to $458 a month

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.040
by the end of this year.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.500
One year! That is a huge increase.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:33.520
But now there's this new drug which is like half the cost.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.720
Hopefully they won't keep raising the price of that a hundred percent every year.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.380
Thing number 4

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:41.160
I really hate it when I'm watching a show on my computer on full screen,

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.740
and then the show fades to black,

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.040
and then suddenly I can see my reflection in the monitor,

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.360
and I see that slack, dull face just staring at itself.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.300
I just want to snap out of it and go do something with my life,

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.080
but then I know that I can't, because you know, I'm in the middle of a show,

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:56.740
Thing number 5

00:01:56.740 --> 00:02:00.360
Katherine brought this up the other day and I just want to bring it the idea to light

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.000
Why don't we have waterbeds that double as aquariums?

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.540
Thing number 6

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:09.420
One time, I left a pot of ramen noodles boiling, and then all the water boiled away,

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.200
and then the ramen noodles caught on fire.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.200
Thing number 7

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.780
We might think that the Superbowl is a big deal here in America, but, hockey by percentages,

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:24.740
is a much bigger deal in Canada, where around 80% of the population watched the final Olympic hockey game.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.580
Air Canada had to delay a flight

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:30.620
because the passengers refused to get on board while the hockey game was still going on.

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:34.080
And check out this graph of Edmonton's water use during the Olympic hockey final.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.920
Tha-I-yeah, that's a lot of people not peeing, and then having to pee.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:39.340
Thing number 8

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:45.000
The winners of the Harry Potter Alliance Helping Haiti Heal raffle have been announced!

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.780
So if you participated in that raffle, you will have received an email saying that you won a thing if you won a thing.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.660
But the nerdfighter-related prizes were:

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:57.220
A song by me about you was won by Samantha.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.340
Samantha, I'm gonna write a song about you.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.580
Signed copies of all of my cds was won by Samuel in Pennsylvania.

00:03:03.580 --> 00:03:07.820
The John Green 3 book package was won by Flower Child Headbands,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:10.520
which I'm sure is probably exactly what it sounds like.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:16.940
And a 1,000 word short story written by a New York Times bestselling author on the topic of your choosing,

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:19.340
was won by Nancy from San Francisco.

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:23.840
We will be contacting all of you soon. Congratulations, Helping Haiti Heal!

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.760
5 planes full of aid supplies are already on their way,

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:30.876
You didn't forget to be awesome, John, I will see you on Monday.

